# Email Provider Integration

## OAuth Flow
- Kick off authentication by requesting `GET /auth/oauth/google`; redirect the browser to the returned URL (`window.location.href = url`).
- Handle connection completion by refreshing accounts after the backend redirects to `/email/auth/success` or `/email/auth/failure`.
- Use `EmailAuthModal` for account linking; surface loading (`isAuthenticating`) and error states from `useEmailProvider`.

## Accounts & Labels
```typescript
const {
  accounts,
  selectedAccountId,
  selectAccount,
  labels,
  userLabels,
  systemLabels,
  selectLabel,
} = useEmailProvider();
```
- Fetch connected accounts via `GET /email/accounts`; keep the selected account in provider state so the sidebar updates consistently.
- Refresh labels on account change; store label metadata in provider-specific Recoil atoms if it needs cross-component access.

## Conversations & Messages
- List conversations with pagination using placeholder endpoints in `frontdesk/frontdesk-endpoints.ts` until real backend routes are ready.
- Support search (`query`), paging (`pageToken`), and label filters when calling backend APIs.
- When invoking `handleSendEmail`, include `replyToMessageId` and `threadId` so replies stitch into the right thread.
- Provide inline reply (quick send) and modal composer (rich reply) pathways; reuse `EmailComposer` for complex compose flows.

## Messaging UX
- Show empty states when no account connected; enable `Connect Gmail Account` CTA that opens `EmailAuthModal`.
- Present `star`, `archive`, `delete` actions in the conversation list; wire them to service methods or stub with TODO logs until backend endpoints exist.
- Maintain `composerDraft` in hook state and clear once send resolves successfully.

## Error & Loading Handling
- Expose `accountsLoading`, `labelsLoading`, `conversationsLoading`, and `isSending`; drive skeletons/spinners accordingly.
- Surface API errors (`accountsError`, `labelsError`, `conversationsError`, `authError`) via `Alert` components placed near the affected UI.
- Guarantee fallback UI for missing data (e.g., no selected conversation → show `FrontdeskEmptyState`).
